WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.102
[music playing]

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.838
NARRATOR: On the border
with Ancient Nubia,

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.975
Ramses built another massive
monument, the mountain

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.544
temple of Abu Simbel.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.647
Colleen has come here
searching for clues about how

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.484
Ramses's military
skill contributed

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.819
to the success of his empire.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:26.760
This is, like, the greatest
hits of Ramses's victories.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.461
[music playing]

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.598
NARRATOR: Ramses consolidated
his empire in the south

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.835
and pushed north to confront his
powerful enemies, the Hittites.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.837
[music playing]

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.708
In temples all over
Egypt, he recorded

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.544
his victory against
the Hittites,

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:46.279
or so he wanted us to think.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.648
[music playing]

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:53.186
NARRATOR: Around 1300
BC, the Egyptians

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.789
fought their arch
rivals, the Hittites,

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:59.893
at the fortress city of
Kadesh in possibly the largest

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.928
chariot battle in history.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.832
The light Egyptian chariots had
the edge over the heavy Hittite

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.234
war machines.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:11.204
Ramses recorded the
victory as a massacre.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:14.240
But in reality, it
was more of a draw.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.977
The two kings agreed a truce,
resulting in the world's

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:21.481
first recorded peace treaty.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.316
[music playing]

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:27.487
It enabled the Egyptians to
spend all of their resources

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:31.291
on peacetime pursuits,
building massive constructions

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:37.363
like this, and usher in
a golden age for Egypt.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.366
NARRATOR: Instead of waging
costly military campaigns,

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:45.205
Ramses built his success
through a mastery of diplomacy.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.540
But to win the hearts
of his citizens,

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.077
he still needed to depict
himself as a mighty warrior.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.179
[music playing]

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.850
He's on his chariot
alone, with the reins

00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:02.088
tied behind his back so that
he's free to shoot his bow.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.390
We know that this is a
little bit of propaganda

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.826
because even the
hieroglyphic tax says

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:11.998
that his shield-bearer Mena was
riding in the chariot with him.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.768
NARRATOR: Ramses was a master
of ancient public relations,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.371
happy to bend the truth
to promote an image which

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.772
would appeal to his people.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.208
[music playing]

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.647
In the temple's inner
sanctum, Colleen

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:31.818
discovers another secret
of Ramses's success.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:35.221
Here, by placing his statue
between the greatest gods

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:40.026
of Egypt, Ramses used a
clever trick of the light

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.828
to engineer his own divinity.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.197
[music playing]

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:48.001
Twice a year, the sun
rays reach all the way

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:53.773
through the temple, illuminating
these figures in the sanctuary.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.009
[music playing]

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.777
NARRATOR: Colleen
believes Ramses used

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:01.648
this solar alignment to
convey a powerful message,

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:06.719
that he was the living
embodiment of the Sun God.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:13.026
Truly, here at Abu Simbel,
Ramses II is not just a king,

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.727
he is a god.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.497
[music playing]

